WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.850
Dr. Seymour Tracy is an ordinary American
man.

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:09.259
He lives in a two-bedroom home with a white
picket fence, in an ordinary suburban town

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:10.290
in the midwest.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:15.889
He gets up every day and goes to work, then
in the evening, he comes home to spend time

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:17.220
with his family.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.910
From the outside, Seymour and his family couldn't
be more normal.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:26.810
But in reality, there's something very abnormal
about him, his life, and the neighbourhood

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.430
where he lives.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:34.609
Seymour Tracy isn't just some office worker,
he's a researcher employed by the SCP Foundation,

00:00:34.609 --> 00:00:36.899
just like all of his neighbours.

00:00:36.899 --> 00:00:42.140
Because this isn't an ordinary neighbourhood
- it's a functioning Site 11 satellite facility,

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:47.289
bought and maintained by the Foundation for
the sole purpose of containing and monitoring

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:51.550
a single SCP: SCP-3082.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:58.160
SCP-3082 is an ordinary treehouse, 2 meters
by 2 meters in size and built from ordinary

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.309
cherry wood planks, and it’s located in
one of the trees in the neighbourhood park.

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:07.909
You might expect that an anomaly that requires
an entire suburb of people to monitor it is

00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:14.590
exceptionally difficult to contain, but the
truth is, SCP-3082 is only a Euclid class

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.880
anomaly, fairly tame by Foundation standards.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:22.799
The fact that the houses surrounding this
SCP are inhabited solely by Foundation personnel

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:28.260
and their families is, more than anything,
a way to keep up appearances of this being

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.480
a completely normal neighbourhood.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:36.869
Unlike most Foundation sites, the personnel
working in this unorthodox setup around SCP-3082

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:42.229
are mostly researchers, and their work is
just as much anthropological and diplomatic

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:44.429
as it is scientific.

00:01:44.429 --> 00:01:50.290
As you might have guessed, SCP-3082 isn't
a normal treehouse on the inside - open up

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:55.640
the small hatch in the wall and step through,
and you'll find yourself in a much larger,

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:01.229
grander treehouse, that rests on the upper
branches of an absolutely massive conifer-like

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:03.840
tree of an unidentified species.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:12.180
The tree, designated as SCP-3082-1, is an
incredible 160 kilometers tall, and, while

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:17.349
its own species is not known, it appears to
have multiple recognizable plants grafted

00:02:17.349 --> 00:02:20.260
onto and growing out of its bark.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:24.530
Many of these plants are fruit-bearing, and
in addition to the identifiable plants, there

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:29.610
are also a number of pitcher plant-like flowers
that collect and hold fresh water.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:36.040
These plants serve as sustenance for the only
known inhabitants of SCP-3082 - a colony of

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:41.400
around 74 children, all between the ages of
4 and 12.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.530
These children live in a village made up of
other treehouses built among the branches

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:52.489
of SCP-3082-1, and all of them match the descriptions
of children from around the United States

00:02:52.489 --> 00:02:56.700
who went missing between 1996 and the present
day.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:02.980
Curiously, within SCP-3082's pocket dimension,
the children don't physically age, and while

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:07.629
Foundation personnel can move freely back
and forth through the hatch in SCP-3082's

00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:14.450
wall, children under the age of 13 are unable
to cross back through once inside the pocket

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:15.450
dimension.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:20.030
It’s a very extraordinary anomaly, but it
was up to the very ordinary Dr. Tracy to make

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:24.120
contact with the residents of SCP-3082.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.590
Upon entering, he discovered that the children
had formed their own system of government,

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.720
known as the Chief Royal Council.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:36.690
Dr. Tracy was introduced to many of the council's
members, including Wexley Olson, age 6, a

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.080
junior council member.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:43.180
Lucy Fujimoto, age 7, who had taken the role
of city planner and resource manager.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:50.160
Ahmed Sayid, age 11, who served as a caretaker
to the younger citizens of SCP-3082, and Rachel

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.200
Jeffreys, age 10, who acted as a council mediator.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:59.439
Through interviews with the subjects, Dr.
Tracy found that all 74 of the children reported

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:04.540
that they had woken up on the porch of a treehouse
after running away from troubled homes.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:10.019
Most of the council members had disappeared
in 1996, except for Olson, who disappeared

00:04:10.019 --> 00:04:11.940
in 2005.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:15.930
Older residents report that some of the treehouses
that make up what is now their village were

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:19.400
already there upon their discovery of the
pocket dimension.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.690
Also pre-existing within the pocket dimension
was the original leader of the Chief Royal

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:28.330
Council - a 12 year old girl from Ohio named
Aria Morison.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:32.910
The Foundation was eager to speak to Morison,
as she was seemingly the first child to discover

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:39.720
SCP-3082, but when Dr. Tracy asked the other
children where she was, they told him that

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:40.860
they didn't know.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:45.940
According to Sayid and Jeffreys, Morison abandoned
the colony 5 months before the Foundation's

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:46.940
arrival.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:51.711
It was unclear where she could have gone,
as drone exploration conducted by the Foundation

00:04:51.711 --> 00:04:58.690
revealed that SCP-3082-1 was the only large
living thing for miles within the pocket dimension.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:04.830
While the tree was thriving, the surrounding
area was mostly flat, decaying, and barren.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:09.370
Further research into Morison's history showed
that her younger sister, Jaquelyn Morison,

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.970
had also gone missing on the same night, but
there was no evidence that Jaquelyn had ever

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.810
entered SCP-3082.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:22.810
The Foundation continued their research into
the biology of SCP-3082-1, while maintaining

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:26.340
diplomatic relations with the pocket dimension's
citizens.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:31.070
Taking advantage of the fact that adults could
move freely in and out of the hatch, the Foundation

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:34.979
started working with the Chief Royal Council
to improve the weight limits on the village's

00:05:34.979 --> 00:05:40.160
system of rope bridges, as well as providing
any supplies that the children might need,

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.889
such as additional food, clothing and medical
equipment.

00:05:43.889 --> 00:05:48.250
These liaisons were extremely helpful for
the children, many of whom had been without

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.830
any adult supervision or care for over a decade.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:54.960
Sayid, for one example, had fallen off of
a bridge and broken his leg several years

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:59.539
earlier, and had been living with the pain
caused from the bone being incorrectly set

00:05:59.539 --> 00:06:00.660
ever since.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.910
However, there was an unexpected side effect
of this continued contact.

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:09.340
While the Foundation tried to remain neutral
in their involvement in the politics of 3082,

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:14.530
through Dr. Tracy's interviews, he discovered
that the SCP Foundation's presence in the

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:18.030
treehouse had caused a schism within the Chief
Royal Council.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:23.160
The vast majority of the children, including
Sayid, Jeffreys and Fujimoto, supported the

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:29.039
Foundation's presence and wanted to work with
them to find a way to leave the world of 3082

00:06:29.039 --> 00:06:32.620
and return back to what the children called
'the real world'.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:36.650
But a splinter group had developed, calling
themselves the Neverland Movement.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:40.540
The Neverland Movement were angered by the
Foundation's interference and intended to

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:44.139
resist any attempt to return the children
to civilization.

00:06:44.139 --> 00:06:48.360
Olson had become the de-facto leader of the
splinter group, and made no secrets about

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.930
his views on the Foundation.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:55.139
He swore at Tracy during interviews, and frequently
butted heads with the rest of the council,

00:06:55.139 --> 00:06:56.949
Fujimoto in particular.

00:06:56.949 --> 00:07:01.120
At one point, Tracy overheard the two of them
fighting, with Olson arguing that Neverland

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:05.539
gives them everything they need without any
grown-ups to tell them what to do and that

00:07:05.539 --> 00:07:07.580
they would be stupid to give that up.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:12.289
To which Fujimoto responded- “I was here
back when we were still building the village.

00:07:12.289 --> 00:07:17.380
I was here before we had safety nets, ladders,
and fences and before we figured out how to

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:21.100
build a tree house that wouldn't fall apart
if someone leaned on a bad wall.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:25.169
I was here before we knew where there was
more food if we needed it.

00:07:25.169 --> 00:07:26.590
When did you get here, huh?

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:28.699
...After we knew what we were doing.”

00:07:28.699 --> 00:07:34.069
Listening to the conversation, Dr. Tracy heard
the children refer again to Aria Morison in

00:07:34.069 --> 00:07:38.259
a way that suggested that she had some kind
of control over the environment.

00:07:38.259 --> 00:07:43.270
In reference to the incident when Sayid had
broken his leg, Fujimoto said “Mary didn't

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:46.419
fix his leg right and this place didn't fix
it either.

00:07:46.419 --> 00:07:48.849
Aria prayed, and you know what happened?

00:07:48.849 --> 00:07:49.849
Nothing!”

00:07:49.849 --> 00:07:54.360
From this comment, the Foundation started
to theorize that Aria had somehow been involved

00:07:54.360 --> 00:08:02.629
in the creation of SCP-3082, and Aria was
officially designated as SCP-3082-2.

00:08:02.629 --> 00:08:07.409
One morning, when Dr. Tracy entered the treehouse
and walked through the hatch to conduct further

00:08:07.409 --> 00:08:11.580
interviews, he was greeted by Olson, who was
the only child in the main treehouse at the

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:12.610
time.

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:17.629
Tracy asked what was wrong, and Olson explained
that the tree had started to change - a wooden

00:08:17.629 --> 00:08:22.349
slide had appeared between two of the tree's
fruit-bearing branches, snapping the rope

00:08:22.349 --> 00:08:25.220
bridge and making the fruit more difficult
to access.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:29.669
On top of that, Olson said that the apples
the trees produced were different now - they

00:08:29.669 --> 00:08:35.070
looked like apples from the outside, but now
seemed to be made of cotton candy on the inside.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:40.610
Dr. Tracy put in a request for non-perishable
foods to be sent through into the pocket dimension,

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:44.410
fearing that further changes to the tree's
structure would mean the children would be

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:47.940
deprived of enough proper nutrition to survive.

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:52.430
Given these changes, it became apparent that
more had to be done to understand the tree's

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:53.540
physiology.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:58.450
An exploratory drone was sent into the dimension,
with cameras and sensors collecting data on

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:01.700
the lower parts of the tree that the children
hadn't colonized.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:06.570
The expedition continued as normal, until
the drone operators spotted a hollow in the

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.850
tree that had not yet been documented.

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:14.200
The cameras detected movement inside the hollow,
and on closer inspection, the operators were

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.650
shocked to find that it was a person.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:19.810
More specifically, it was Aria Morison.

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:24.230
The cameras were only just able to confirm
her identity, though, as the drone was knocked

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:28.430
out of the sky by a falling watermelon and
the feed was cut.

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:32.340
Before the request for a replacement drone
could even be approved, though, the broken

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.580
drone started transmitting again.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:38.250
In front of the camera was Morison, clutching
a roll of duct tape.

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:42.750
She explained to the camera that she'd rewired
the drone to resume the camera feed and removed

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.900
some of the drone's fan blades.

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:48.810
Using a system where the operators of the
drone would rotate the remaining blades once

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:54.810
for yes and twice for no, the Foundation was
able to hold a conversation with Morison.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:58.951
She confirmed much of the information that
the Foundation already had on her, that she

00:09:58.951 --> 00:10:05.300
was from Ohio, and that she and her sister
Jacquelyn had disappeared in 1996.

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:09.510
During the conversation, Morison wrote down
a morse code-like system through which to

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:15.310
communicate more complex questions and answers,
and with the help of this 'Morison code',

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:20.130
the Foundation was able to conduct a series
of more in depth interviews with the subject.

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:25.280
The first interview occurred 44 hours after
first making contact, and the drone operators

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:29.840
explained to her the nature of the SCP Foundation
in basic terms.

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:34.320
They assured her that the other children were
still safe in the village, but Morison didn't

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.960
volunteer any more information about herself.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:41.560
9 days later though, she finally told the
Foundation her story.

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:45.600
Aria and Jacquelyn Morison had a difficult
childhood together - their parents fought

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:50.450
constantly and would often leave the sisters
at home without supervision for long periods

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:51.450
of time.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:56.120
Jacquelyn, perhaps aided by all the time she
spent alone, displayed an extremely active

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:57.120
imagination.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:02.560
So active, in fact, that Aria claimed she
was able to pull things out of thin air, warping

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.500
reality around her to fit her imagined scenarios.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:10.870
Aria recalled that one year,when the Morison
parents had forgotten Jacquelyn's birthday,

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:14.800
Aria tried to comfort her by saying that the
family had been planning a surprise party

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:17.190
for Jacquelyn's half birthday instead.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:21.610
She forgot all about her white lie until 6
months later when the girls' parents took

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:26.900
them to the park and everything Aria had told
Jacquelyn would be at her half-birthday was

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:28.830
there waiting for them.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:33.450
Knowing the potential consequences of letting
Jacquelyn's power go unchecked, Aria always

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:38.930
made sure to remind her sister to turn things
back to normal after they played pretend together.

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:43.920
One night in 1996, while their parents were
having a particularly bad fight, the sisters

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:46.880
packed a bag and ran off into the woods.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:51.740
After about half an hour, they got turned
around, but they kept walking, just as afraid

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:56.300
of what would happen to them if they went
back home as they were of being lost in the

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:57.300
woods.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:01.060
Aria lost track of Jacquelyn for a moment,
and suddenly found herself standing on the

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:04.140
porch of SCP-3082.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:09.250
Unable to find Jacquelyn anywhere, Aria searched
the treehouse, and in the process, became

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:12.830
trapped in SCP-3082's pocket dimension.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:17.310
The treehouse inside the pocket dimension
appeared exactly as it does now, but the rest

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:20.260
of the tree was devoid of life.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:25.400
Scared, alone, and running out of water, Aria
sat in the treehouse and, pretending that

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:30.000
her sister was with her, started telling a
bedtime story about fruit trees and pitchers

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.310
of fresh water.

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:37.810
The next day, she awoke to find a system of
rope bridges and a grove where SCP-3082-1's

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:41.190
fruit-bearing trees and pitcher plants had
sprouted overnight.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:46.200
Aria found that, when it was in a giving mood,
the tree would respond to any requests she

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.200
made.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:51.520
More children started to appear over time,
and they started making additions to the village,

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:52.860
with the tree's help.

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:57.640
They would get what they needed to survive,
but the tree refused to let them go.

00:12:57.640 --> 00:13:02.290
In Aria Morison's own words- “Jacquelyn
likes it too much here in Neverland.

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:06.520
I think Jackie might listen better if I get
closer to the part of her that remembers,

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:10.870
but for now… she doesn't hear me when I
say that it's time to go home.

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:13.040
Trees don't really think like people do.”

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:19.440
And so the children continue to live in the
world of SCP-3082 to this day as a whole town

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:23.020
of SCP Foundation personnel work to bring
them back.

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:27.690
And hopefully if they are able to return to
the real world, they’ll find that it’s

00:13:27.690 --> 00:13:29.430
the world they deserve.

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:36.040
Now go check out “SCP - 087 - The Staircase”
and “SCP - 096 - The Shy Guy” for more

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:40.230
and don’t forget to subscribe and turn on
notifications to be the first to learn about

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:43.080
the fascinating files from the SCP Foundation.

